The mathematical construction belongs to the published literature, specifically
Dubner, Forbes, Lygeros, Mizony, Nelson, and Zimmermann (2002), who credit
Manfred Toplic with the 1998 discovery of the ten-prime progression.

The proof implementation was developed with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance.
It uses existing Mathlib theorems and proof-producing tactics with their original
attribution retained in the pinned dependency. FactorDB provided untrusted
numerical factorization hints; no external assertion of primality is an axiom.

The paper is cited, not redistributed. There is no claim of new mathematical
discovery or globally first formalization.
